<article class="env-proposition" id="432242">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/432242">Proposition <span data-tag="432242">5.1.4.9</span>.</a>idempotent completion!universal property of Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor which exhibits $\calD $ as the idempotent completion of $\calC $, and let $\calE $ be an $\infty $-category which is idempotent complete. Then composition with $f$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories $f^{\ast }: \Fun (\calD , \calE ) \rightarrow \Fun (\calC , \calE )$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Without loss of generality, we may suppose that $f$ is the inclusion of a full subcategory. In this case, we combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/65B21B" data-tag="65B21B">5.1.4.7</a>, <a href="/tag/54E672" data-tag="54E672">5.1.4.8</a>, and Proposition <a href="/tag/DD1683" data-tag="DD1683">4.3.2.15</a> to deduce that $f^{\ast }$ is a trivial fibration. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>